{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-81792",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The following triangle illustrates the information given.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/4f5aad8cf0a25781bc08d6ee51b739ecd68f9d2d7a5acc84230ff743739ea533.png)\n\nThe law of sines states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡L}{l}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡N}{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\nn=6,\\,m∠N={36}^{∘},\\,l=9,\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡L}{9} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{36}^{∘}}{6} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡L & =9\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{36}^{∘}}{6} \\\\  & ≈9\\cdot \\frac{0.587\\,79}{6} \\\\  & ≈0.881\\,69,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠L & ≈\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0.881\\,69)≈{61.85}^{∘},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠M & ={180}^{∘}-m∠N-m∠L \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{36}^{∘}-{61.85}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈{82.15}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, another solution to $\\operatorname{sin}⁡L=0.881\\,69$ is given by\n\n$$\nm∠L≈{180}^{∘}-{61.85}^{∘}={118.15}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠M & ={180}^{∘}-m∠N-m∠L \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{36}^{∘}-{118.15}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈{25.85}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, there are two possible triangles, with the following angle measures:\n\n- $m∠L≈{61.85}^{∘},\\,m∠M≈{82.15}^{∘},\\,m∠N={36}^{∘}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/31d18e2602d9acceccea6a0fe672b4c3f992b12c30c4921b3234e2f22cc454af.png)\n\n- $m∠L≈{118.15}^{∘},\\,m∠M≈{25.85}^{∘},\\,m∠N={36}^{∘}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/b51c7e3eada7a8e44b0fb9912b95684d77b40e49f8c6bde7859e73f20c6d9f40.png)\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
